<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Boyacá Department</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Boyacá</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Boyacá <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">Department</a> is a department of central Colombia in the Eastern Ranges of the Andes, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunja">Tunja</a>. Its high plateau was the northern heartland of the Muisca, whose towns included Hunza, Sugamuxi and Tundama, the modern Tunja, Sogamoso and Duitama. It gives its name to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-boyaca">Battle of Boyacá</a> of 1819, which secured the independence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-granada">New Granada</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/boyaca-department.jpg" alt="Boyacá Department" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Davemor · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ritacuba_.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
